  "scenario_result": [
    "The interrupted-write fixture covers restart before replacement, restart after replacement but before commit, new-file creation, an outside edit that conflicts with the expected revision, and the Windows replacement-backup state.",
    "Recovery resumes only when the on-disk revision matches the journal's expected revision, recognizes a write already at its next revision, and leaves conflicting outside bytes intact while requiring attention.",
    "Pending incoming and prior recovery images remain protected until the journal reaches a terminal state; startup recovery runs before the Markdown scan and its outcome is available to the UI.",
    "Existing multi-file rename recovery tests passed, including preservation of outside edits and restoration of every original byte in the transaction fixture."
